https://github.com/RFnexus/modem73

Windows binaries come from the experimental Win32 port:
https://github.com/RFnexus/modem73-win

Release archives include a modem73 built from the upstream source at a
pinned tag (.github/workflows/modem73.yml, v2.5.0 for both) with small
patches added. Network audio (`-d tcp:HOST:PORT`), which WeeChat Radio uses
to carry a Bluetooth radio's audio (VR-N76 / VR-N7600) into modem73 with no
sound card, is upstream since v2.5.0 and needs no patch.

- `patches/wcr-features.patch` (Linux and macOS): the `audio_in_db`,
  `audio_in_peak_db` and `audio_in_clip_pct` levels in the control port's
  status and a `get_spectrum` command, which feed the level meter and the
  waterfall; TX level down to 1 % (upstream stops at 5 %); and in CSMA sync
  mode a contention slot at least as long as modem73 needs to hear another
  station's frame (#241), so two stations in nearby slots do not collide;
  and network audio waits 250 ms without capture before it paces transmit
  itself (upstream waits 20 ms, the same as wcr's Bluetooth bridge tick, so
  every slightly late block logged "no capture data", #359).
- `patches/wcr-features-win.patch` (Windows): the same CSMA sync slot and
  network audio changes.
- `patches/encode-before-busy-test.patch` (Linux and macOS): modem73
  encodes a frame to audio before its CSMA busy test instead of after
  `CSMA: Channel clear`, so PTT keys straight after the clear (on a Pi 3
  the encode took about 1 s, long enough for another station to key in
  that gap). It logs `TX: frame encoded before the busy test (N ms)`.

The patches are under the same Unlicense as modem73. That binary is not
Apache-2.0.
macOS archives also include the `libs/` folder (`@executable_path/libs`).
See the Unlicense at the upstream repository.

`wcr` downloads a missing modem73 from its **own** WeeChat Radio release
tag, never from `/releases/latest`. The release workflow hashes the modem73
asset it bundles and builds that SHA-256 into `wcr` (`WCR_MODEM73_SHA256`),
so the download always matches the bundled copy. Builds made outside the
release workflow fall back to release `v0.1.79` and the hashes in
`sha256.json` next to this file.
